    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_dec100595cddf914baffcacc1c0295974c6ffac0b18d6917a32e9baf20bcdba0",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The Wigner transform reorganizes the same zeta state into diagonal number-state Wigner terms and off-diagonal Moyal terms: the former track photon-number populations, while the latter carry coherence between distinct number states. This representation gains an experimentally reconstructible phase-space geometry of interference without, in this span, establishing any later claim about overlap magnitudes, complex phase recovery, or zeta zeros. Its use depends on the Wigner/Moyal identities cited from the appendix, and exact numerical coefficients in the extracted equation remain to be scan-verified.",
