    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_217a82a39cb1ef1b785c7b8e8d0b09c6da778be6f9d5bf4641678d5a2026fae1",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Accuracy is observable-relative in the source's effective model: the weighted return amplitude can remain close even when individual effective phases do not closely reproduce the logarithmic generator, because phase agreement is modulo 2π, high-index discrepancies are downweighted, and termwise errors can cancel. Restricting the coupling to a low-degree even polynomial then turns this tolerance into a finite coefficient-selection example whose output agrees qualitatively before the generator does.",
