    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_21b4b0485f3ef9b231fa85dc35fd7192d0f07b301ef4b32fe61c9280937e7651",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source moves through an information hierarchy in phase space: an overlap of real single-state Wigner functions returns a fidelity and therefore only |ζ|², whereas the cross-state Moyal symbol retains relative phase and integrates directly to a complex scalar product. The same refinement is instantiated first for the Dirichlet zeta-state pair and then for the weighted two-branch Riemann–Siegel construction.",
