    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_5a84e74ce1706fbd56311d0ae67aa05381c7619770e4cab60baa835a1d095ff9",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "At σ=1/2, the complementary field parameters in the engineered reference coincide and β becomes a pure phase, so the reference factorizes. That algebraic simplification makes every reference Wigner-matrix entry the same field profile up to constants and conjugate phase factors; when paired with the evolved state's matrix, the resulting kernel is k-symmetric and gives a particularly legible signed-cancellation picture near the sampled zero.",
